+
+## Where the pieces came from
+
+This fork is a merge, and every part has an owner:
+
+| Capability | Source |
+|---|---|
+| Everything else, and the base | [ggml-org/llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) |
+| Ternary 128-group format and kernels | [PrismML-Eng](https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp) |
+| Expert streaming from disk | [Tiiny-AI / PowerInfer](https://github.com/Tiiny-AI/PowerInfer) |
+| AMD weight formats, positional-encoding fix | [charlie12345 / ROCmFPX](https://github.com/charlie12345/ROCmFPX) |
+| Host prefetch patches | thecodacus (unmerged community pull requests) |
+| TurboQuant weight formats | the TurboQuant project |
+
+Every patch in [`patches/series/`](../patches/series/) names its source repository and commit.
+
+## When something does not work
+
+1. **A model will not load.** If the error mentions a type or block size, it is a format the build
+   does not have compiled — see the rebuild section above. If it mentions tensor offsets, the
+   file's type tag does not match its layout.
+2. **A crash on Windows with `q4_0`, `iq4_nl` or `mxfp4`.** Fixed here; if you see it, you are on
+   stock upstream or an older build. Details in [`FINDINGS.md`](FINDINGS.md) F-01.
+3. **A feature seems to do nothing.** Check it actually engaged rather than assuming. Repack
+   allocates its own buffer and logs it; streaming logs its working set. Two of our own early
+   comparisons were meaningless because the code never ran in either arm.
+4. **Numbers do not match ours.** They should not. Ours are from one machine, stated on every
+   figure. Measure on yours.
